WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:12.957
The next morning, Heidi opened her eyes.

2
00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:16.920
She was in a high bed facing two windows covered by long curtains.

3
00:00:17.721 --> 00:00:22.365
It was very different from her bed in the hayloft, with its view down the valley through the

4
00:00:22.425 --> 00:00:23.286
hole by her bed.

5
00:00:24.046 --> 00:00:26.168
Heidi jumped out of bed and ran to a window.

6
00:00:26.889 --> 00:00:30.652
The curtains were too heavy for her to push aside, so she crawled under them.

7
00:00:31.308 --> 00:00:33.469
Behind the curtains, the window was too high.

8
00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:37.090
She could only just peer out and couldn't find a way to open it.

9
00:00:37.831 --> 00:00:39.351
Suddenly there was a knock on her door.

10
00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:42.333
"Breakfast is ready," said the maid.

11
00:00:42.773 --> 00:00:46.014
Heidi had no idea what she was expected to do, so she waited.

12
00:00:46.854 --> 00:00:48.675
Shortly after, Fraulein appeared.

13
00:00:49.275 --> 00:00:50.916
"What is the matter with you, Heidi?"

14
00:00:51.476 --> 00:00:52.297
she said angrily.

15
00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:55.238
"Don't you understand what breakfast is?

16
00:00:56.018 --> 00:00:57.099
Come along at once!"

17
00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:00.240
Heidi had no difficulty understanding that.

18
00:01:00.756 --> 00:01:02.497
She followed Fraulein downstairs.

19
00:01:03.137 --> 00:01:06.398
The windows in the dining room were also too high for her to see out of.

20
00:01:06.959 --> 00:01:09.320
Heidi was starting to feel like she was in a prison.

21
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.921
Clara had been at the breakfast table for a while and was smiling cheerfully.

22
00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:17.623
Heidi didn't know it, but Clara was often lonely and glum.

23
00:01:18.243 --> 00:01:22.905
Now that Heidi was staying with her, Clara was looking forward to all sorts of new fun.

24
00:01:24.906 --> 00:01:30.288
As soon as the children were alone, Heidi asked, "How can I open a window in my bedroom?"

25
00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.224
"You can ask Sebastian.

26
00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:35.625
He'll be happy to open one for you," Clara assured her.

27
00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:37.526
Heidi was very relieved.

28
00:01:38.406 --> 00:01:41.247
While the girls were eating breakfast, Clara's tutor arrived.

29
00:01:41.687 --> 00:01:45.088
Fraulein took him aside and told him all her worries about Heidi.

30
00:01:45.428 --> 00:01:50.229
He was a patient man and said that regular teaching would soon help her catch up to Clara.

31
00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:54.570
After breakfast, the girls joined him in the study and started their lesson.

32
00:01:55.611 --> 00:02:00.292
A little while later, Fraulein was walking past the study door when she heard a huge crash.

33
00:02:01.044 --> 00:02:02.766
"Look at the state of things!"

34
00:02:03.146 --> 00:02:05.208
exclaimed Fraulein when she opened the door.

35
00:02:05.228 --> 00:02:10.172
"Tablecloth, books, work basket, everything covered in ink.

36
00:02:10.792 --> 00:02:12.694
It was Heidi's fault, I suppose!"

37
00:02:12.714 --> 00:02:18.058
"Yes, but it was all an accident," said Clara.

38
00:02:18.078 --> 00:02:22.221
"Heidi heard the carriages passing outside, and they startled her."

39
00:02:22.702 --> 00:02:25.144
Fraulein was angry, but did not punish Heidi.

40
00:02:26.085 --> 00:02:31.709
Later that afternoon, while Clara took her nap, Heidi asked Sebastian where she could go to see out

41
00:02:31.889 --> 00:02:32.750
over the whole city.

42
00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:37.272
"You would have to climb to the top of a church tower," said Sebastian.

43
00:02:38.153 --> 00:02:42.095
With that in mind, Heidi set off in search of the highest tower she could find.

44
00:02:42.675 --> 00:02:46.937
On a street corner, she saw a boy with a hand organ and asked, "Do you know any

45
00:02:46.997 --> 00:02:48.558
churches with high towers?"

46
00:02:48.578 --> 00:02:51.000
"Yes, I know one.

47
00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:54.462
For two pennies, I will show you," the boy said.

48
00:02:54.482 --> 00:02:56.223
"Clara will pay you.

49
00:02:56.483 --> 00:02:58.304
She has money," Heidi agreed.

50
00:02:58.952 --> 00:03:01.153
"And will you help me find my way back home?"

51
00:03:01.454 --> 00:03:01.974
she asked.

52
00:03:01.994 --> 00:03:04.275
"Yes, for another two pennies."

53
00:03:04.295 --> 00:03:06.557
"Okay," said Heidi.

54
00:03:07.477 --> 00:03:09.778
The boy led her through the streets to an old church.

55
00:03:10.359 --> 00:03:15.201
A priest answered the bell and, holding her hand, led Heidi up the winding stairs.

56
00:03:15.882 --> 00:03:17.783
At the top, Heidi was disappointed.

57
00:03:17.803 --> 00:03:21.345
"I wanted to see the mountains.

58
00:03:21.965 --> 00:03:25.207
All I can see are roofs and towers and chimney tops!"

59
00:03:25.728 --> 00:03:26.208
she said.

60
00:03:27.788 --> 00:03:30.389
"I have something else to show you," said the priest.

61
00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:31.450
"Follow me."

62
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:36.292
At the bottom of the stairs, behind a closet door, he showed her a basket.

63
00:03:36.672 --> 00:03:41.814
Heidi bent down and said with delight, "Oh, look at the sweet little kittens!"

64
00:03:42.274 --> 00:03:43.434
"Would you like to have them?"

65
00:03:43.875 --> 00:03:44.555
asked the priest.

66
00:03:44.955 --> 00:03:46.596
Heidi could hardly contain her joy.
